<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bolesław IV the Curly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1122–<a href="/years/1173">1173</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Boleslaw IV the Curly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bolesław IV the Curly was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masovia">Masovia</a> and from 1146 High Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, holding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> after he and his younger brothers drove out their eldest brother, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wladyslaw-ii-the-exile">Władysław II the Exile</a>. He had to submit to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> after the imperial invasion of 1157. On his death in 1173 his brother Mieszko III succeeded him as senior duke.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iv-the-curly.jpg" alt="Bolesław IV the Curly" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bonio · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:O%C5%82bin-tympanon_fundacyjny-awers.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
